From 7f4b0d8c2f2c8a9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ChatGPT <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PM: genpd: add release callback for genpd device

The generic PM domain embeds a struct device. pm_genpd_init() initializes
it and genpd_free_data() later calls put_device(). Provide a no-op release
callback to avoid the driver-core warning when the device is released.

This patch is based on drivers/base/power/domain.c from
dede94445/geralt-sku6_linux, branch chromeos-r158-v6.1.180.

---
 drivers/base/power/domain.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/base/power/domain.c b/drivers/base/power/domain.c
--- a/drivers/base/power/domain.c
+++ b/drivers/base/power/domain.c
@@ -26,5 +26,10 @@
 #include <linux/debugfs.h>

 #include "power.h"

+static void genpd_provider_release(struct device *dev)
+{
+	/* nothing to be done here */
+}
+
 #define GENPD_RETRY_MAX_MS	250		/* Approximate */
@@ -2122,3 +2127,4 @@ int pm_genpd_init(struct generic_pm_domain *genpd,
 	device_initialize(&genpd->dev);
+	genpd->dev.release = genpd_provider_release;
 	dev_set_name(&genpd->dev, "%s", genpd->name);

--
2.43.0
